## Frequently asked questions

**Where are you based?**

We're based in [Merthyr Tydfil](/web-design-merthyr-tydfil/), South Wales, and work with businesses across Wales and UK-wide.

**How long does a website take?**

Most projects are completed within 7–14 days depending on scope.

**Will my website work on mobile?**

Yes. Every website we build uses mobile-first design.

**Can I update the site myself?**

Yes. We provide full access and training as part of every project.

**How much does web design in Wales cost?**

Our WordPress web design starts from £199 for a one-page website. Larger websites, ecommerce builds, and SEO campaigns are quoted based on the number of pages and the amount of content needed.

**Do you offer affordable web design for new Welsh businesses?**

Yes. We work with start-ups, trades, sole traders, local shops, and service businesses across Wales. If you only need a simple first website, we can keep the build focused and affordable.

**Can one website target multiple Welsh towns?**

Yes, but it needs the right structure. A main website can be supported by focused location pages for important areas such as Cardiff, Swansea, Newport, Llanelli, Wrexham, and Merthyr Tydfil.

